# Project: mydodo (Dodo Mail Client)

## Identity
- **Name**: Dodo (`dodo-mail` on PyPI, v0.2)
- **Author**: Aleks Kissinger <aleks0@gmail.com>
- **License**: GPLv3
- **Repo**: https://github.com/akissinger/dodo
- **Docs**: https://dodomail.readthedocs.io/en/latest/
- **Local dir**: `~/Projects/mydodo` (likely a fork or personal copy — upstream is `dodo`)

## What It Is
Dodo is a graphical, hackable email client built in Python/PyQt6. It provides a
vim-like, keyboard-driven interface on top of the [notmuch](https://notmuchmail.org/)
email indexer. It's inspired by alot and astroid (two other notmuch-based clients).

## Core Philosophy
- Keyboard-oriented with keychord support (e.g. `g g` for top, `t m` to tag marked)
- UNIX philosophy: offloads work to battle-tested CLI tools
- Text-first by default; HTML view is one keystroke away (`H`)
- Fully configurable: `~/.config/dodo/config.py` is exec'd Python that can override
  settings, keymaps, themes, layouts, message filters, and add custom commands
- Non-destructive: all operations go through notmuch tags; no email is ever lost

## Architecture

### Entry Point
`dodo/__main__.py` → `dodo/app.py:main()` → creates `Dodo(QApplication)`, calls `.exec()`

### Class Hierarchy
```
QApplication
 └── Dodo (app.py) — owns everything, holds global commands

QMainWindow
 └── MainWindow (mainwindow.py)
      ├── QTabWidget (tabs)
      │    └── Panel (panel.py) — base class for all panels
      │         ├── SearchPanel (search.py) — search results via notmuch query
      │         ├── ThreadPanel (thread.py) — single thread view
      │         ├── ComposePanel (compose.py) — compose/reply/forward
      │         └── TagPanel (tag.py) — tag browser
      ├── CommandBar (commandbar.py) — bottom command input with tag completion
      └── HelpWindow (helpwindow.py) — keybinding reference (? key)

QAbstractItemModel
 ├── SearchModel (search.py) — wraps `notmuch search --format=json`
 ├── ThreadModel (thread.py) — wraps `notmuch show --format=json`
 └── TagModel (tag.py) — wraps `notmuch search --output=tags`
```

### Module Map
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app.py` | `Dodo(QApplication)`, `SyncMailThread`, `main()` |
| `mainwindow.py` | `MainWindow`: tabs, command bar, window geometry save/restore |
| `panel.py` | `Panel(QWidget)`: base class with keychord handling, dirty tracking, temp dir cleanup |
| `search.py` | `SearchPanel` + `SearchModel`: list threads matching a notmuch query |
| `thread.py` | `ThreadPanel` + `ThreadModel` + message handlers: view a thread's messages |
| `compose.py` | `ComposePanel` + `EditorThread` + `SendmailThread`: compose/reply/forward |
| `tag.py` | `TagPanel` + `TagModel`: browse all notmuch tags with message counts |
| `commandbar.py` | `CommandBar(QLineEdit)`: search/tag input with tag autocomplete and history |
| `keymap.py` | Global + per-view keymaps (`global_keymap`, `search_keymap`, `thread_keymap`, `compose_keymap`, `tag_keymap`, `command_bar_keymap`) |
| `settings.py` | All configurable settings with defaults and docstrings |
| `themes.py` | Theme dicts (Nord, Solarized light/dark, Catppuccin macchiato, Gruvbox light/dark/hard/soft) + `apply_theme()` |
| `util.py` | HTML/text helpers, key string parsing, attachment I/O, message wrapping, CSS generation |
| `helpwindow.py` | `HelpWindow`: renders all keybindings as HTML |
| `pgp_util.py` | PGP/MIME signing and encryption via python-gnupg |

### Data Flow
1. **Search**: `notmuch search --format=json` → `SearchModel` → `QTreeView` (4 cols: date, from, subject, tags)
2. **Thread**: `notmuch show --format=json --include-html` → `ThreadModel` → message list (QTreeView) + message body (QWebEngineView via custom URL scheme `message:`)
3. **Compose**: raw email string → external editor (via `EditorThread`) → `SendmailThread` pipes to sendmail command → saved to Maildir sent folder
4. **Sync**: `SyncMailThread` runs `offlineimap` then `notmuch new` on a timer

### Custom URL Schemes
- `message:html` / `message:plain` — serves message body to embedded QWebEngineView
- `cid:<content-id>` — serves embedded images from MIME parts
- `mailto:` — intercepted to open compose panel

### Configuration System
- Defaults in `dodo/settings.py` (module-level variables with docstrings)
- User overrides in `~/.config/dodo/config.py` (exec'd at startup)
- PyQt6.QtCore and PyQt6.QtWidgets are already imported in config.py scope
- Can override: settings, theme, keymaps, layouts, message2html filters, command bar modes

### External Tools Required
- `notmuch` — email indexing and searching
- `offlineimap` or `mbsync` — IMAP to Maildir sync
- `msmtp` — SMTP sendmail-compatible client
- `w3m` — HTML to plaintext conversion
- `python-gnupg` (optional) — PGP/MIME signing/encryption

### Python Dependencies
- PyQt6 >= 6.2
- PyQt6-WebEngine >= 6.2
- bleach >= 5.0
- setuptools >= 42 (build only)

### Build Output
A pre-existing build exists in `build/lib/dodo/` — the package has been installed
from this directory via `pip install .`

## Key Bindings (Summary)
- `?` — help
- `h/l` — previous/next tab
- `x/X` — close panel / close all
- `c` — compose
- `/` — search bar
- `t t` / `t m` — tag / tag marked
- `I/U/F/T` — inbox / unread / flagged / tags view
- Vim-style navigation: `j/k`, `C-d/C-u`, `g g/G`, `<space>` to mark+advance
- Thread view: `r/R` reply, `C-f` forward, `H` toggle HTML, `M` toggle list mode
